From e4ff052d8d14b277593697c127df4ca75b73fb4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bo Fang <quic_bofang@quicinc.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Aug 2022 00:42:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] waylandsink: support ubwc modifier and
 zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 version3

To support UBWC, must upgrade zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 from ver1 to ver3. Then,
dmabuf protocol could contain modifier information. UBWC and other information,
like security, could be transmitted from wayland client to wayland server
through this modifier channel.

To interact with upstream plugin, introduced "compression" field in caps. This
"compression" could be "linear" or "ubwc", based on wayland server reported
modifier capability.

Added NV12_10LE32 UBWC format support, it also named as Q12A or TP10. HW
decoder won't output NV12_10LE32 linear.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Change-Id: I09bcca6202def252bd0f7e580d2d170d8a5c4b5d
Signed-off-by: Bo Fang <quic_bofang@quicinc.com>
Signed-off-by: Lily Li <quic_lali@quicinc.com>
---
